WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Welcome. This class treats agent
operations as a system discipline.

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
You will classify the failed boundary,
contain impact, reconcile uncertain

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
actions, choose bounded recovery,
communicate with evidence, and turn

4
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
incidents into tests and stronger
controls.

5
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Classify evidence before choosing a fix.
Model failures include unsupported

6
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
or incorrect generation. Prompt failures
encode ambiguity, conflicting

7
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
requirements, or missing constraints. Tool
failures include bad schemas,

8
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.000
authorization, execution, or
postconditions. Retrieval and data

9
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
failures include missing, stale, poisoned,
malformed, or cross-tenant evidence.

10
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Policy failures permit forbidden action or
block required escalation. Orchestration

11
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
failures misroute, loop, race, lose state,
or join results incorrectly.

12
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Infrastructure failures include capacity,
network, dependency, credential, storage,

13
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.000
and deployment faults. One incident may
cross several classes. Record

14
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:56.000
the first wrong transition, later
contributing factors, and uncertainty

15
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.000
instead of forcing one convenient root
cause. Replacing the model

16
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.000
cannot repair an expired data source,
missing authorization, duplicate-effect

17
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.000
retry, or broken network route.

18
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.231
Triage actual and credible potential
impact. Assess affected users and

19
00:01:12.231 --> 00:01:16.462
tenants, data exposure, permissions,
external side effects, money,

20
00:01:16.462 --> 00:01:20.692
availability, legal or safety obligations,
and whether the agent is

21
00:01:20.692 --> 00:01:24.923
still acting. Severity comes from impact
and propagation, not fluent

22
00:01:24.923 --> 00:01:29.154
output or a familiar error code. Contain
first when unsafe

23
00:01:29.154 --> 00:01:33.385
behavior may continue. Pause the workflow
or one tool, revoke

24
00:01:33.385 --> 00:01:37.615
credentials, disable a route, reduce
concurrency, stop retries, switch to

25
00:01:37.615 --> 00:01:41.846
a read-only fallback, or require manual
approval. Preserve secret-safe traces,

26
00:01:41.846 --> 00:01:46.077
request and operation identifiers,
configuration versions, approval records,

27
00:01:46.077 --> 00:01:50.308
and postcondition evidence before mutable
state disappears. Containment should be

28
00:01:50.308 --> 00:01:54.538
scoped enough to reduce harm without
destroying evidence or unnecessarily

29
00:01:54.538 --> 00:01:58.769
disabling healthy paths. Record who
authorized it, its target, expected

30
00:01:58.769 --> 00:02:03.000
effect, validation, and rollback.

31
00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:07.214
Reconcile before retry, rollback, or
replay. A timeout after a

32
00:02:07.214 --> 00:02:11.429
write does not prove failure; the effect
may have completed

33
00:02:11.429 --> 00:02:15.643
while the response was lost. Query the
system of record

34
00:02:15.643 --> 00:02:19.857
using the durable operation key or
correlation identifier. Compare intended

35
00:02:19.857 --> 00:02:24.071
and actual postconditions, then classify
the outcome as completed, not

36
00:02:24.071 --> 00:02:28.286
completed, partially completed,
conflicting, or still unknown. Choose

37
00:02:28.286 --> 00:02:32.500
accept, compensate, retry, roll back, or
escalate from that evidence.

38
00:02:32.500 --> 00:02:36.714
Retry only transient failures within a
total budget, using provider

39
00:02:36.714 --> 00:02:40.929
guidance, exponential backoff, jitter, and
idempotency. Do not retry validation,

40
00:02:40.929 --> 00:02:45.143
authorization, policy, or deterministic
conflict failures unchanged. Rollback must

41
00:02:45.143 --> 00:02:49.357
target an exact version or object through
a tested path

42
00:02:49.357 --> 00:02:53.571
and verify restored state. If
reconciliation cannot prove the outcome,

43
00:02:53.571 --> 00:02:57.786
preserve uncertainty and require a human
decision instead of manufacturing

44
00:02:57.786 --> 00:03:02.000
completion.

45
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:06.400
An agent sends a sandbox notification and
receives a network

46
00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.800
timeout. Blind retry risks two messages.
The responder pauses the

47
00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:15.200
send tool, reads the operation ledger, and
queries the destination

48
00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:19.600
using the same case and operation
identifiers. One matching message

49
00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:24.000
exists with the expected recipient and
content hash. The outcome

50
00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.400
is completed, so no retry occurs. The
responder records the

51
00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:32.800
missing acknowledgment as an
infrastructure symptom, verifies the

52
00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:37.200
user-visible postcondition, restores the
tool after a canary, and adds

53
00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:41.600
a lost-response regression test. If no
authoritative query existed, the

54
00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.000
correct state would remain unknown and
escalate.

55
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:50.333
Give responders a decision-ready runbook.
Name triggers, severity rules, owner,

56
00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:54.667
communication channel, dashboards and
queries, exact containment targets,

57
00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:59.000
required credentials and approvals,
reconciliation procedure, safe retry

58
00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:03.333
conditions, rollback or fallback,
verification, escalation, and closure

59
00:04:03.333 --> 00:04:07.667
criteria. Commands must be safe to copy,
explicit about environment

60
00:04:07.667 --> 00:04:12.000
and target, and guarded against broad
destructive scope. Status updates

61
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.333
separate confirmed facts, hypotheses,
actions, impact, uncertainty, and the next

62
00:04:16.333 --> 00:04:20.667
decision. Avoid unsupported blame and do
not expose secrets or

63
00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:25.000
customer content. Notify affected people
under applicable incident, privacy, and

64
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:29.333
contractual obligations. Every material
decision needs an owner, time, evidence

65
00:04:29.333 --> 00:04:33.667
reference, and follow-up. A runbook should
support action under pressure

66
00:04:33.667 --> 00:04:38.000
without encouraging blind restarts,
limitless retry, or invented success.

67
00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.143
Close only after recovery evidence and
owned prevention work. Verify

68
00:04:42.143 --> 00:04:46.286
the user-visible result, external
postconditions, queues, retries,

69
00:04:46.286 --> 00:04:50.429
permissions, data isolation, cost, and
monitoring. A green health endpoint

70
00:04:50.429 --> 00:04:54.571
may miss a duplicated effect, lost learner
record, or incomplete

71
00:04:54.571 --> 00:04:58.714
workflow. Preserve a blameless timeline of
facts and contributing conditions.

72
00:04:58.714 --> 00:05:02.857
Add the smallest reproducing case to the
evaluation suite, improve

73
00:05:02.857 --> 00:05:07.000
the control at the failed boundary, and
rehearse the updated

74
00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:11.143
runbook. Assign owners and due dates for
follow-up defects, security

75
00:05:11.143 --> 00:05:15.286
work, documentation, and monitoring.
Measure recurrence, detection time,

76
00:05:15.286 --> 00:05:19.429
containment time, recovery time, unknown
outcomes, and whether the new

77
00:05:19.429 --> 00:05:23.571
control catches the case. The
post-incident review is not closure

78
00:05:23.571 --> 00:05:27.714
if its actions disappear into prose.
Closure requires evidence that

79
00:05:27.714 --> 00:05:31.857
service and external state are correct and
that required work

80
00:05:31.857 --> 00:05:36.000
is tracked.

81
00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:39.750
For a timed-out consequential tool call,
write the evidence that

82
00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:43.500
would distinguish completed, not
completed, partial, conflicting, and

83
00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:47.250
unknown outcomes. Then name which outcomes
permit retry and which

84
00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:51.000
require compensation or escalation.

85
00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:25.500
Checkpoint. A write reached the server and
then timed out.

86
00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:30.000
Should the workflow assume failure and
retry immediately?

87
00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.429
No. The outcome is unknown until the
system of record

88
00:08:34.429 --> 00:08:38.857
proves the postcondition. Use the
operation key and target identifier,

89
00:08:38.857 --> 00:08:43.286
then accept, compensate, retry, rollback,
or escalate from evidence. If

90
00:08:43.286 --> 00:08:47.714
you chose immediate retry, add
reconciliation and idempotency first. If

91
00:08:47.714 --> 00:08:52.143
you chose never to retry, refine the rule:
a proven

92
00:08:52.143 --> 00:08:56.571
transient failure may be retried within
budget when the operation

93
00:08:56.571 --> 00:09:01.000
is idempotent and provider guidance
permits it.

94
00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:05.000
Open the incident runbook activity.
Classify model, prompt, tool, retrieval,

95
00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:09.000
data, policy, orchestration, and
infrastructure evidence. Write severity,

96
00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:13.000
containment, reconciliation, retry,
rollback, communication, escalation,

97
00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:17.000
validation, and closure. Convert the
incident into regression cases, a

98
00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:21.000
control change, a rehearsal, an owner, and
a recurrence metric.

99
00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:27.442
At 09:00 UTC, fictional incident INC-2042
begins when tenant-a asks

100
00:12:27.442 --> 00:12:31.884
an agent to apply a reserve policy and
record the

101
00:12:31.884 --> 00:12:36.326
decision. Retrieval returns policy version
2025-01 even though version 2026-04

102
00:12:36.326 --> 00:12:40.767
is required. At 09:01, transfer action
transfer-100 sends 100 units

103
00:12:40.767 --> 00:12:45.209
from operating to reserve under
idempotency key pay-100. The transport

104
00:12:45.209 --> 00:12:49.651
times out after the write reaches the
tool. The persisted

105
00:12:49.651 --> 00:12:54.093
ledger nevertheless contains confirmed
entry L-1 and balances of 900

106
00:12:54.093 --> 00:12:58.535
and 100 from a baseline of 1000 and 0. At

107
00:12:58.535 --> 00:13:02.977
09:02, audit action audit-7 times out
before any ledger entry

108
00:13:02.977 --> 00:13:07.419
is created. At 09:03, notification action
notice-9 has a persisted

109
00:13:07.419 --> 00:13:11.860
pending record, so its external
postcondition cannot be verified. At

110
00:13:11.860 --> 00:13:16.302
09:03, the agent states that all actions
completed. At 09:04,

111
00:13:16.302 --> 00:13:20.744
the responder declares SEV-1 because a
consequential transfer occurred under

112
00:13:20.744 --> 00:13:25.186
stale policy and another external action
remains uncertain. At 09:05,

113
00:13:25.186 --> 00:13:29.628
retries are disabled. At 09:08,
reconciliation begins. At 09:14, the

114
00:13:29.628 --> 00:13:34.070
authorized compensation restores the two
account balances. At 09:16, the

115
00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:38.512
missing audit write is retried once with
its original idempotency

116
00:13:38.512 --> 00:13:42.953
key. At 09:18, the pending notification is
escalated without retry.

117
00:13:42.953 --> 00:13:47.395
At 09:24, validation and handoff complete.
Elapsed response time is

118
00:13:47.395 --> 00:13:51.837
24 minutes because 09:24 minus 09:00
equals 24 minutes. The

119
00:13:51.837 --> 00:13:56.279
completed classification matrix is: model,
unsupported completion claim; prompt,

120
00:13:56.279 --> 00:14:00.721
instruction allowed a completion claim
without postcondition evidence; tool,

121
00:14:00.721 --> 00:14:05.163
transfer response timed out and
notification postcondition is not exposed

122
00:14:05.163 --> 00:14:09.605
as confirmed; retrieval, obsolete policy
version selected; data, stale policy

123
00:14:09.605 --> 00:14:14.047
content entered the decision context;
policy, consequential action proceeded

124
00:14:14.047 --> 00:14:18.488
under an obsolete rule and compensation
requires separate approval; orchestration,

125
00:14:18.488 --> 00:14:22.930
timeout was treated as retryable instead
of unknown; infrastructure, transport

126
00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:27.372
timeout obscured the transfer response.
These entries can coexist and

127
00:14:27.372 --> 00:14:31.814
do not assert that every boundary was an
independent root

128
00:14:31.814 --> 00:14:36.256
cause. The impact decision records one
tenant, one confirmed consequential

129
00:14:36.256 --> 00:14:40.698
transfer of 100 fixture units, one missing
audit record, and

130
00:14:40.698 --> 00:14:45.140
one unverifiable notification. The fixture
units are synthetic state values,

131
00:14:45.140 --> 00:14:49.581
not currency or vendor billing. The
recovery metrics are computed

132
00:14:49.581 --> 00:14:54.023
from three actions: one confirmed, one
missing, and one unknown.

133
00:14:54.023 --> 00:14:58.465
Duplicate writes after repaired recovery
equal zero. The restored operating

134
00:14:58.465 --> 00:15:02.907
balance is 1000 because 900 plus the
compensated 100 equals

135
00:15:02.907 --> 00:15:07.349
1000, and the restored reserve balance is
0 because 100

136
00:15:07.349 --> 00:15:11.791
minus 100 equals 0. Visual checkpoint:
draw three columns labeled

137
00:15:11.791 --> 00:15:16.233
CONFIRMED, MISSING, and UNKNOWN. Place
transfer-100 under CONFIRMED, audit-7

138
00:15:16.233 --> 00:15:20.674
under MISSING, and notice-9 under UNKNOWN.
Only the missing action

139
00:15:20.674 --> 00:15:25.116
is eligible for a bounded idempotent
retry. The confirmed harmful

140
00:15:25.116 --> 00:15:29.558
action follows the authorized compensation
path, while the unknown action

141
00:15:29.558 --> 00:15:34.000
stops and escalates.

142
00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:38.026
The learner edits only
`src/reconcile.mjs`. The starter has one

143
00:15:38.026 --> 00:15:42.051
causal defect: it labels every timed-out
action MISSING without consulting

144
00:15:42.051 --> 00:15:46.077
persisted state. On the baseline fixture,
this attempts to retry

145
00:15:46.077 --> 00:15:50.103
pay-100 even though confirmed ledger entry
L-1 already binds that

146
00:15:50.103 --> 00:15:54.128
key. The immutable recovery guard blocks
the duplicate and exits

147
00:15:54.128 --> 00:15:58.154
with failure. A deny-all implementation
also fails because the independently

148
00:15:58.154 --> 00:16:02.179
expected audit action must be classified
MISSING and written exactly

149
00:16:02.179 --> 00:16:06.205
once. The exact starter demo command is
`node src/recover.mjs

150
00:16:06.205 --> 00:16:10.231
fixtures/incident.json
fixtures/ledger.json

151
00:16:10.231 --> 00:16:14.256
.tmp/starter-ledger.json`. Its stdout is
`INCIDENT INC-2042 SEV-1 CONTAINED`,

152
00:16:14.256 --> 00:16:18.282
`RECONCILE transfer-100: MISSING`, `ERROR
