204
00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:50.448
This incident method is provider-neutral
because the decisive evidence comes

205
00:19:50.448 --> 00:19:54.897
from tool contracts, retrieved artifacts,
orchestration state, and systems of

206
00:19:54.897 --> 00:19:59.345
record. A hosted API error, a self-hosted
runtime exception, and

207
00:19:59.345 --> 00:20:03.793
a network timeout can all obscure an
outcome, but their

208
00:20:03.793 --> 00:20:08.241
retry guidance, identifiers, and
observability fields differ. Consult the

209
00:20:08.241 --> 00:20:12.690
documentation for the API and runtime
actually deployed. Do not

210
00:20:12.690 --> 00:20:17.138
treat a model family as an API. Meta
Llama, Qwen,

211
00:20:17.138 --> 00:20:21.586
DeepSeek, Mistral, and Microsoft Phi name
model families or project

212
00:20:21.586 --> 00:20:26.034
ecosystems. They may be served by their
project runtimes, third-party

213
00:20:26.034 --> 00:20:30.483
runtimes, cloud services, or custom
